### name: stmt.text-identity.derived-pass-through.sqlite
--- dialect
sqlite
--- options
{"strict":true}
--- bindings
{"R":{"kind":"relation","from":"r","fields":{"CAT":{"kind":"column","column":"cat","type":"TEXT"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> MAP(RECORD("cat", _["cat"])) .> BUCKET(_["cat"], RECORD("cat", _K, "n", COUNT(_)))
--- expect
SELECT CAST("_sub1"."cat" AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY AS "cat", COUNT(*) AS "n" FROM (SELECT "cat" AS "cat" FROM "r") "_sub1" GROUP BY CAST("_sub1"."cat" AS TEXT) COLLATE BINARY
--- note
A direct field projection preserves its declared type through the derived table;
forgetting TEXT silently inherits a schema's NOCASE/RTRIM grouping semantics.
===
